-- The Parley (a preamble, not a term; it does not alter anything below) --

Some code is built like a fortress, guarded clause by clause. This isn't
that. This is a Parley: an open hand held out before any conflict has to
happen. Take what you need. Build what you mean to build. Deal fairly with
the people whose work you're building on.

Every path of knowledge, once walked and understood, is worth sharing
freely with whoever is willing to walk it next — that is the debt every
builder owes the ones who opened the way before them. Keep the notice
below intact, and the Parley is honored.

